{
  "$comment": [
    "Walk back U6's crystal move and QSPI bottom-layer reroute.",
    "",
    "Both fixes needed the same 0.96 mm lane between the Inner2 keepout edge",
    "(x=166.129) and U2's west pads (x=167.090). Moving X1 0.5 mm east to open",
    "OSC_OUT's escape pushed the crystal's case-ground guard from x=165.959 to",
    "166.45, which is where the QSPI escape vias have to sit; and routing the bus",
    "bottom-side left the router no room to escape U2's pads at all, so it dropped",
    "six vias INSIDE them. An unplugged via in an SMD pad wicks solder off the",
    "joint during reflow -- on the flash's six signal pins that is a dead board.",
    "",
    "Assembly beats EMI margin, and the two cannot coexist here, so the crystal",
    "goes back to its imported position and 2-via route, and QSPI goes back to the",
    "imported escape geometry, which is the only arrangement where both fit.",
    "The guard restore is bounded to the crystal's own region so the rest of GND",
    "is untouched.",
    "",
    "Kept from U6: the CAN and USB fixes, which are independent of this lane."
  ],
